1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,824
On a Saturday, Aziz logs in to the mobile bank with his password and a code.

2
00:00:04,874 --> 00:00:07,512
The password is right, and the code is right.

3
00:00:07,562 --> 00:00:09,576
The mobile bank opens for him.

4
00:00:09,626 --> 00:00:11,568
He wants to send money to his mother.

5
00:00:11,618 --> 00:00:13,440
But the money does not move.

6
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:19,688
His password and his code are both right, so why are they not enough for money?

7
00:00:19,738 --> 00:00:25,784
Lesson 1 showed this Saturday as one step of his journey, and it drew the map of the platform.

8
00:00:25,834 --> 00:00:31,040
This lesson gives the three words behind that step, and it explains what a level is.

9
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:32,912
Each word checks a different thing.

10
00:00:32,962 --> 00:00:35,168
The first word is authentication.

11
00:00:35,218 --> 00:00:39,032
Authentication checks that this is the owner of the account.

12
00:00:39,082 --> 00:00:44,888
Aziz shows something he knows, his password, and something he has, his phone, which gets the code.

13
00:00:44,938 --> 00:00:47,528
Notice what authentication does not say.

14
00:00:47,578 --> 00:00:50,720
It does not say that this is Aziz from the state records.

15
00:00:50,770 --> 00:00:54,176
It says only that this is the person who registered the account.

16
00:00:54,226 --> 00:01:00,320
A stranger can register with his own phone and his own password, and he passes authentication every day.

17
00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:02,648
The second word is identity proofing.

18
00:01:02,698 --> 00:01:07,544
Identity proofing checks that this is a real person in the state records.

19
00:01:07,594 --> 00:01:11,960
heeyID does it in one way only: MyID, in the mobile bank.

20
00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:16,208
MyID compares a live face and a passport with the state records.

21
00:01:16,258 --> 00:01:19,160
Proofing is slow, and Aziz does it one time.

22
00:01:19,210 --> 00:01:23,672
Authentication is fast, and it happens at every login.

23
00:01:23,722 --> 00:01:29,792
The most common mistake in identity work is to treat a strong login as proof of a person.

24
00:01:29,842 --> 00:01:34,064
A password and a code prove that you hold the account, not who you are.

25
00:01:34,114 --> 00:01:36,224
The third word is authorisation.

26
00:01:36,274 --> 00:01:39,608
Authorisation decides what this session may do, now.

27
00:01:39,658 --> 00:01:44,960
The rule is simple: money data and the verified identity need level two.

28
00:01:45,010 --> 00:01:48,032
Cards, accounts and transfers are money data.

29
00:01:48,082 --> 00:01:51,056
The app's own data needs only level one.

30
00:01:51,106 --> 00:01:52,952
That rule stopped the transfer.

31
00:01:53,002 --> 00:01:55,376
heeyID has three levels.

32
00:01:55,426 --> 00:01:58,280
At level zero, nothing is verified.

33
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:01,640
At level one, a code verified the phone number.

34
00:02:01,690 --> 00:02:06,992
At level two, MyID proved the person, and the phone number is confirmed as his.

35
00:02:07,042 --> 00:02:09,944
Only the check for a level gives that level.

36
00:02:09,994 --> 00:02:14,888
No operator and no setting puts a person at level two without MyID.

37
00:02:14,938 --> 00:02:18,560
A person has a level, and each session has a level too.

38
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:22,568
A session in the mobile bank gets level two only on the trusted phone.

39
00:02:22,618 --> 00:02:28,472
The trusted phone is the one phone where Aziz passed MyID, and where TAF confirmed his SIM card.

40
00:02:28,522 --> 00:02:31,232
Only a session on that phone moves money.

41
00:02:31,282 --> 00:02:36,296
On that Saturday, Aziz is still at level one, and his phone is not trusted.

42
00:02:36,346 --> 00:02:38,168
The app does not refuse him.

43
00:02:38,218 --> 00:02:41,720
It names the level that it needs, and the check that gives that level.

44
00:02:41,770 --> 00:02:45,896
First his consent, then MyID, then the check of his phone number.

45
00:02:45,946 --> 00:02:49,328
Aziz passes all three, and he is at level two.

46
00:02:49,378 --> 00:02:53,480
His phone becomes the trusted phone, and the transfer to his mother goes.

47
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:58,544
Same person, same password: the level and the phone make the difference.

48
00:02:58,594 --> 00:03:03,920
Keycloak issues the tokens for the app, and each token holds the level of its session.

49
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:06,824
heeyID has no token format of its own.

50
00:03:06,874 --> 00:03:12,608
The tokens follow two open standards, and their names are in every identity document.

51
00:03:12,658 --> 00:03:17,432
OAuth 2.1 says how an app gets a token, and what the token lets it do.

52
00:03:17,482 --> 00:03:21,776
OpenID Connect sits on top of it, and adds who logged in, and how.

53
00:03:21,826 --> 00:03:25,400
The mobile bank reads the level of the session, and decides.

54
00:03:25,450 --> 00:03:29,096
So why did the right password and the right code not move his money?

55
00:03:29,146 --> 00:03:34,232
Because they pass only authentication, and money needs level two on the trusted phone.

56
00:03:34,282 --> 00:03:37,184
Authentication checks the owner of the account.

57
00:03:37,234 --> 00:03:41,408
Identity proofing checks the real person, one time, with MyID.

58
00:03:41,458 --> 00:03:45,488
Authorisation decides what each session may do, from its level.

59
00:03:45,538 --> 00:03:50,264
Today, Aziz is at level two, and his phone is the money phone.

60
00:03:50,314 --> 00:03:55,712
Lesson 3 shows the perimeter: where the platform runs, and which services it may call.
